  "fallback": {
    "text": "A stack and a queue are both lists with restricted access, but the access ends differ. A stack pushes and pops at the top, so the most recently inserted item is removed first: last in, first out (LIFO). A queue enqueues at the rear and dequeues at the front, so the earliest inserted item is removed first: first in, first out (FIFO). If 1, 2, 3 are inserted into both, the stack removes 3, 2, 1 while the queue removes 1, 2, 3. The same insertion order therefore gives opposite removal orders. A stack is not a queue, and the first inserted item is not always removed first."
  },
